# DarDesign frontend environment
#
# The backend is a FastAPI service (POST /redesign) exposed through a
# cloudflared / ngrok tunnel from the Kaggle notebook. The tunnel URL ROTATES
# EVERY SESSION. You normally never edit this by hand — instead run:
#
#   npm run dev:tunnel https://<new-url>.trycloudflare.com
#
# which writes .env.local, checks /healthz, and starts `next dev` on :3000
# (the only origin the backend's CORS allowlist accepts by default).
# Read by src/lib/api.ts, which falls back to http://localhost:8000 when unset.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://your-current-subdomain.trycloudflare.com

# Where accounts, saved designs and ratings are stored. Unset, it follows
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL — one backend does everything, as before.
#
# Set it to a backend on THIS machine to keep the data pure local: the SQLite
# file and the saved images/ folder then live on your disk and survive the GPU
# session being wiped, while /redesign and /restyle still run on the tunnel.
# Start that local backend (no GPU needed — it only stores):
#
#   set DARDESIGN_LIGHT=1
#   python -m uvicorn backend.main:app --port 8000
#
# dev:tunnel rewrites only the NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL line, so this one survives.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DATA_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
